tiles: row, col, height, and gold amount.
tile(0, 0, 10, 0).
tile(0, 1, 10, 0).
tile(1, 0, 10, 10).
tile(1, 1, 10, 0).

spawn point.
spawn(0, 0).

exit location.
exit(1, 1).

treasure mapping: from tile (0,1) a treasure leads to tile (1,0).
treasure(0, 1, 1, 0).

current water level.
waterLevel(0).

agent with id, starting row, col, and initial gold.
agent(1, 0, 0, 0).

A tile is flooded if the water goes above the height
flooded(Row, Col) :-
    tile(Row, Col, Height, _),
    waterLevel(WL),
    WL > Height.

The agent is only safe when they are on a tile that is not flooded
safe(AgentID) :-
    agent(AgentID, Row, Col, _),
    tile(Row, Col, Height, _),
    waterLevel(WL),
    WL =< Height.

Get the agents current gold
agentGold(AgentID, Gold) :-
    agent(AgentID, _, _, Gold).

The agent can only exit when the coordinates match one that is an exit
reachedExit(AgentID) :-
    agent(AgentID, Row, Col, _),
    exit(Row, Col).

Queries
?flooded(row, col) 
?safe(1)
